Copyleft components
-------------------

* espeak-ng (GPL-3.0-or-later)
  Installed from Debian packages in the Docker image and used by the Kokoro
  phonemizer for grapheme-to-phoneme conversion. Bundled as a shared library
  by the espeakng-loader wheel (the loader itself is MIT).
  https://github.com/espeak-ng/espeak-ng

* phonemizer-fork (GPL-3.0-or-later)
  Transitive dependency of misaki/kokoro (speech extra, Docker image).
  https://pypi.org/project/phonemizer-fork/

* FFmpeg libraries bundled in PyAV (av) wheels (LGPL-2.1-or-later; some
  builds may enable GPL-licensed components)
  PyAV itself is BSD-3-Clause. faster-whisper uses it to decode audio.
  https://pyav.org/ and https://ffmpeg.org/legal.html

* libsndfile (LGPL-2.1-or-later)
  Bundled in soundfile wheels (soundfile itself is BSD-3-Clause) and
  installed from Debian packages in the Docker image.
  https://libsndfile.github.io/libsndfile/

* zeroconf (LGPL-2.1-or-later)
  Mesh extra and Docker image; imported only when the mesh is enabled.
  https://github.com/python-zeroconf/python-zeroconf

* num2words (LGPL-2.1)
  Transitive dependency of misaki/kokoro (speech extra, Docker image).
  https://github.com/savoirfairelinux/num2words

* certifi (MPL-2.0) and tqdm (MPL-2.0 AND MIT)
  Transitive dependencies (Hugging Face tooling, HTTP clients).

Operator-supplied components
----------------------------

* Piper TTS runtime and voices. Qantara does not install the Piper runtime;
  current piper-tts releases are GPL-3.0-or-later. Each Piper voice model has
  its own license stated in its model card; review it before redistribution.
* Speech and language models downloaded at first use (faster-whisper/Whisper
  weights, MIT; Kokoro-82M weights, Apache-2.0; spaCy en_core_web_sm, MIT) and
  any Ollama or other LLM model you pull carry their own licenses.

Notable permissive components
-----------------------------

* PyTorch (BSD-3-Clause and bundled third-party licenses), CPU build from
  https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cpu in the Docker image.
* CTranslate2 and faster-whisper (MIT), onnxruntime (MIT), Kokoro and misaki
  (Apache-2.0), spaCy and thinc (MIT), Hugging Face transformers, tokenizers
  and huggingface-hub (Apache-2.0), NumPy (BSD-3-Clause with bundled
  OpenBLAS and compiler runtime libraries), mcp (MIT), httpx (BSD-3-Clause).
* Python and the python:3.12-slim Docker base image (PSF-2.0 and Debian
  package licenses; see /usr/share/doc/*/copyright inside the image).

Redistributing the Docker image, or a bundle that includes the speech extra,
means redistributing the components above under their respective licenses,
including making corresponding source available where the GPL/LGPL require it.
